      "writtenOn": "2015-05-07T12:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can ignoring the exception cause a leak? The framework resources, routing tables, rules, etc. associated with a given network are only freed in handleAsyncChannelDisconnected. That happens if ConnectivityService receives a CMD_CHANNEL_DISCONNECTED. If we ignore the NullPointerException, will ConnectivityService still get CMD_CHANNEL_DISCONNECTED?\n\nAsyncChannel doesn\u0027t seem to provide a way to know if the channel is actually disconnected, so the options I see here are either to make the asyncChannel non-final (but we\u0027d probably want to make it private as well), or to restructure the code such that the cleanup is done when CS decides to tear down the network, not when the AsyncChannel responds that the channel is disconnected after CS has disconnected it.",
